4. **Pigeons**: Three pigeons each ate 3 fries, so they collectively ate \(3 \times 3 = 9\) fries. Therefore, before the pigeons ate, there were \(18 + 9 = 27\) fries.
5. **Seagull**: The seagull ate half the amount Dave did. Dave ate 14 fries, so the seagull ate \(14 / 2 = 7\) fries. Thus, before the seagull ate, there were \(27 + 7 = 34\) fries.

